| Element names in small letters, namespace prefixes separated
| The net effect of this table is that the case
| of all element names following "<" have been downcased and any elements
| of the form <xy:element have been transformed to <xy-ns><element.
| ---
| 1;1 2003-4-23 J E Sullivan, from daielc 1;1 2003-4-18
| 2;1 2010-12-20/jes: Allow for the possibility that "native" the program commands in TXX
|     form, including [es~...] and [ee~...] as well as [<] and [>] commands, may
|     already be present in the input, and if so should be copied through
|     without interpretation.  (Earlier xmlproc may do this in the program as of date.)
| ---
| States:
|   1 = in general text
|   4 = within a nonprocessing tag after "<" & before space
|   5 = within a nonprocessing tag after "</" & before space
|  10 = inside |028 ... |031 (native txx) the program command (added 2010-12-20)
| ---
| Rules for state 1:
<?~<?~1~ | copy processing instruction ignoring "<"
</~</~1~5~ | sense beginning of end-tag
<~<~1~4~ | otherwise sense beginning of tag
